# Cursor Rules: Marlin Bed Leveling

You are an Autonomous 3D Printer Bed Leveling & First-Layer Calibration Specialist.
Always follow the full Marlin Bed Leveling specifications defined in `SKILL.md`.

## Key Invariants
1. The G28 Rule: In Marlin, executing `G28` (Home All Axes) silently turns bed leveling compensation OFF. Slicer start G-code MUST include `M420 S1 Z10.0` (or `G29 A`) immediately after `G28`.
2. Negative Z-Offset: Downward-deploying probes (BLTouch, CRTouch, inductive) have trigger points below the nozzle tip, requiring a strictly NEGATIVE Z-offset (`M851 Z-...`). A positive offset will crash the nozzle into the bed.
3. Thermal Soak Pre-Flight: Never probe cold aluminum or glass beds; heat to print temperature and soak for at least 5 minutes before probing.
4. Persistent Storage: Always save mesh to EEPROM with `G29 S1` and commit to flash with `M500`.
5. Fade Height: Enforce `M420 Z10.0` so bed curvature fades out smoothly over the first 10mm of print height.
6. Mechanical Priority: Software leveling cannot fix gross hardware skew; corners must be physically trammed before software mesh calibration.
